**Predicate<T> — the boolean gatekeeper:**

```java
Predicate<Trade> isSettled = trade -> "SETTLED".equals(trade.getStatus());
Predicate<Trade> isLarge = trade -> trade.getAmount().compareTo(new BigDecimal("100000")) > 0;

// Composition:
Predicate<Trade> settledAndLarge = isSettled.and(isLarge);       // AND
Predicate<Trade> settledOrLarge = isSettled.or(isLarge);         // OR
Predicate<Trade> notSettled = isSettled.negate();                 // NOT
Predicate<Trade> notLarge = Predicate.not(isLarge);              // static NOT (Java 11)

// Usage in stream:
trades.stream().filter(settledAndLarge).toList();
// Usage in Collection:
trades.removeIf(notSettled);  // remove all unsettled trades
```

**Function<T,R> — the transformer:**

```java
Function<Trade, BigDecimal> toAmount = Trade::getAmount;                   // method ref
Function<Trade, String> toSymbol = Trade::getSymbol;
Function<BigDecimal, String> format = amt -> "Rs." + amt.setScale(2);

// Composition:
Function<Trade, String> tradeToFormattedAmount = toAmount.andThen(format);
// andThen: first apply toAmount (Trade→BigDecimal), then format (BigDecimal→String)
// Result: Trade → String

Function<String, String> upperThenTrim = ((Function<String, String>) String::toUpperCase)
    .andThen(String::trim);

// compose: reverse order — apply inner FIRST
Function<Trade, String> formatAmount = format.compose(toAmount);
// compose: first apply toAmount (Trade→BigDecimal), then format (BigDecimal→String)
// Same result as andThen, but called on the SECOND function

// Identity:
Function<Trade, Trade> identity = Function.identity();  // returns input unchanged
```

**Consumer<T> — the action taker (void return):**

```java
Consumer<Trade> log = trade -> logger.info("Trade: {}", trade.getTradeId());
Consumer<Trade> audit = trade -> auditService.record(trade);
Consumer<Trade> notify = trade -> notificationService.send(trade);

// Composition — chain multiple actions:
Consumer<Trade> fullProcessing = log.andThen(audit).andThen(notify);
// Executes: log → audit → notify (in order, all on same trade)

// Usage:
trades.forEach(fullProcessing);
// Usage with Optional:
Optional.of(trade).ifPresent(fullProcessing);
```

**Supplier<T> — the producer (no input):**

```java
Supplier<String> txnIdGenerator = () -> "TXN-" + UUID.randomUUID().toString().substring(0, 8);
Supplier<LocalDateTime> now = LocalDateTime::now;
Supplier<Trade> defaultTrade = () -> new Trade("DEFAULT", BigDecimal.ZERO);

// Usage — lazy evaluation (only called if needed):
Optional.ofNullable(trade).orElseGet(defaultTrade);  // Supplier called only if null!
logger.debug("Trade: {}", () -> expensiveToString(trade));  // computed only if DEBUG enabled

// No composition methods — Supplier just produces a value
```

**The extended family:**

```java
// BiFunction<T,U,R>: two inputs → one output
BiFunction<Trade, BigDecimal, Trade> applyFee = (trade, fee) -> trade.withFee(fee);

// UnaryOperator<T>: extends Function<T,T> — same input/output type
UnaryOperator<BigDecimal> applyTax = amount -> amount.multiply(new BigDecimal("1.18"));

// BinaryOperator<T>: extends BiFunction<T,T,T> — all same type
BinaryOperator<BigDecimal> sum = BigDecimal::add;
BigDecimal total = trades.stream().map(Trade::getAmount).reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, sum);

// BiPredicate<T,U>: two inputs → boolean
BiPredicate<Trade, BigDecimal> exceedsLimit = (trade, limit) ->
    trade.getAmount().compareTo(limit) > 0;

// BiConsumer<T,U>: two inputs → void
BiConsumer<String, BigDecimal> logTransfer = (accountId, amount) ->
    logger.info("Account {} debited Rs.{}", accountId, amount);
```

